  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">DE DOCTRINA IESVITOGRAPHIA, IN QVA</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">RHYTHMIS OMNIA FERE, QVAE HVCVSQVE</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">DE IESVITIS DIXIMVS, COMPREHENDVNTVR.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">O Pulentas Civitates,</l>
    <l n="5">Vbi sunt commoditates,</l>
    <l n="6">Semper quaerunt isti patres.</l>
    <l n="7">Claras aedes, bonum vinum,</l>
    <l n="8">Bonum panem, bonum linum,</l>
    <l n="9">Et pallium tempestivum.</l>
    <l n="10">Indiae Galli, Capones,</l>
    <l n="11">Turdi, lepores, pavones,</l>
    <l n="12">Sunt horum patrum buccones.</l>
    <l n="13">Pingui carne vitulina,</l>
    <l n="14">Non bovina, sed ovina,</l>
    <l n="15">Horum plena est coquina.</l>
    <l n="16">Ambiunt ubique primum,</l>
    <l n="17">Non admittunt peregrinum,</l>
    <l n="18">Nec surgunt ad matutinum.</l>
    <l n="19">Vivunt una loviales-</l>
    <l n="20">Dies agunt feriales.</l>
    <l n="21">Quot optarent esse tales?In</l>
    <l n="22">singulos speculantur,</l>
    <l n="23">Et ubique perscrutantur,</l>
    <l n="24">Quid vel agant vel loquantur.</l>
    <l n="25">Confessores curiosi,P-</l>
    <l n="26">raedicatores verbosi,</l>
    <l n="27">Et doctores fastuosi.</l>
    <l n="28">Solliciti de gloria-</l>
    <l n="29">Semper, &amp; de pecunia,</l>
    <l n="30">Et augenda familia.</l>
    <l n="31">Sui summi laudatores,</l>
    <l n="32">Aliorum despectores,</l>
    <l n="33">Et omnium sunt Censores.</l>
    <l n="34">Ex cohorte iuventutis-</l>
    <l n="35">Illos agunt blandimentis,</l>
    <l n="36">In hos saeviunt tormentis.</l>
    <l n="37">Qui nobiles, qui formosi,</l>
    <l n="38">Divites, ingeniosi,</l>
    <l n="39">Sunt Iesuitis pretiosi.</l>
    <l n="40">Istos sibi praedestinant-</l>
    <l n="41">In illos flagris ferinam-</l>
    <l n="42">Exercent carnificinam.</l>
    <l n="43">Si successio speratur,</l>
    <l n="44">Haec societas laetatur,</l>
    <l n="45">Et qui finquit, praedicatur.</l>
    <l n="46">Si cui caligant oculi,</l>
    <l n="47">Circumstant ripam lectuli</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">Animam sunt habituri,</l>
    <l n="49">Illi bonis potituri.</l>
    <l n="50">Ad illos institutio</l>
    <l n="51">Spectat vel substitutio,</l>
    <l n="52">Vel delegata portio.</l>
    <l n="53">Nam semper ob causam piam,</l>
    <l n="54">Ad augendam familiam</l>
    <l n="55">Detrahunt Falcidiam.</l>
    <l n="56">O vulpinam sanctitatem!</l>
    <l n="57">Praedicando charitatem</l>
    <l n="58">Subducunt haereditatem.</l>
    <l n="59">Sunt audaces ad petendū,</l>
    <l n="60">Prompti sunt ad capiendum,</l>
    <l n="61">Habiles ad succedendum</l>
    <l n="62">Norunt blanda cantilena</l>
    <l n="63">Cum doctrina Christiana,</l>
    <l n="64">Allicere aliena.</l>
    <l n="65">Heus tu bone confitere,</l>
    <l n="66">Sed o nostri miserere,</l>
    <l n="67">Si salutem vis habere.</l>
    <l n="68">Nil habemus ut videtis,</l>
    <l n="69">Date nobis quae habetis,</l>
    <l n="70">Centuplum accipietis.</l>
    <l n="71">Si quem contigit donasse.</l>
    <l n="72">Redi saepe, semper race,</l>
    <l n="73">Absolvo te, vade in pace.</l>
    <l n="74">Hi periti mendicantes,</l>
    <l n="75">Sunt quasi nil habentes,</l>
    <l n="76">Et omnia possidentes.</l>
    <l n="77">Eminent inter clericos,</l>
    <l n="78">Imperant inter laicos,</l>
    <l n="79">Excellunt inter aulicos.</l>
    <l n="80">Heu quot ex istis patribus</l>
    <l n="81">Spretis spiritualibus,</l>
    <l n="82">Incumbunt saecularibus!</l>
    <l n="83">Martem norunt animare,</l>
    <l n="84">Et tumultus suscitare,</l>
    <l n="85">Inter Reges, &amp; sedare.</l>
    <l n="86">In occulto multa tractant:</l>
    <l n="87">Quae vel ipsum Papam celant</l>
    <l n="88">Quid non istae vulpes tentant</l>
    <l n="89">Multa mere ridicula,</l>
    <l n="90">Nobis velut oracula</l>
    <l n="91">Sua iactant miracula.</l>
    <l n="92">Versipelles, gloriosi</l>
    <l n="93">Victores, seditiosi</l>
    <l n="94" type="foot" para="true">Iesuitae, daemon, angeli. Hi, vel ille morituri</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The right half of the page and the lower lines are cut off or blank in this part; the last visible line is partly cut. Dubious readings: "Pulentas" (Opulentas, initial O large woodcut-like), "Ambiunt ubiq;" and "Animam sunt habituri" fragment at top right. The lower-left verse fragment is centred below the column, underlined in print. The cut-off left part of the page is not transcribed. Doubtful: "potituri", "donasse", "race" read as printed.</notes>
</page>
